Getting blasted:

    When you pick up (or wish for) or wield certain artifacts, you will
be blasted by their power.  This happens when the artifact is restricted
("-" in the "can name" column) AND:

   1. the artifact is intelligent and
        its character class or alignment is different from your own,
OR
   2. the artifact's alignment is different from your own
        (1 in 4 chance).

If the artifact is intelligent, and both its alignment and its class
are different from yours, the object will also evade your grasp.
Otherwise, if you don't mind being blasted now and then, you can use
the artifact.

** For these purposes, Excalibur does not discriminate between character
classes.
*** If the player is playing a priest, the alignment of the Mitre of
Holiness is the same as the priest's initial alignment.

The power of the blast can be up to 4d10 hp, depending on whether the
artifact is intelligent and on whether you are magic resistant.


Invocation:

    Most quest objects do something special when invoked.  Some toggle
a property, such as invisibility.  Others perform a service.  Both
kinds of invocation are limited; you have to wait a certain number of
moves between invocations.  However, if you've turned a property on,
you don't have to wait to turn it off.  Once it's turned off, you do
have to wait before you can turn it on again.  The number of moves you
have to wait is on the order of a hundred, and increases with your
experience level.


Explanation of special effects:

  dungeon teleport - allows you to teleport to (the closest level in)
        any dungeon you've already visited.  You get to pick from a menu.

  healing - restores half of your hp deficit.

  restore magical energy - restores half of your energy deficit.

  half damg, half spdm - reduces damage (physical or magical, respectively)
        to your person by half.

  speak - apparently not implemented yet.

  Magicbane - can probe, stun, scare, or purge (= cancel) a monster.
        The chance of these special attacks occuring goes down
        as the weapon is enchanted.


